    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0441" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">858.9111 RR/43.12.02: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-02">December 2,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received December 3—7:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3908. Swedish politics. Our 3899.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d443-f1"/> Swedish
                    Foreign Office announces today Foreign Minister Guenther yesterday made the
                    following <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> German Minister Stockholm:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Swedish Government learns with greatest concern of measures against
                            students, teachers, Oslo University. It cannot refrain from making
                            urgent request measures be stopped especially announced intention deport
                            students. In interest continued Swedish-German relations, Government
                            appeals German Government comply with deeply felt desire Swedish
                            people.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
